# =============================================================================
# Raspberry Pi 4 / BCM2711 — U-Boot boot script, DOM0_OS=zephyr
#
# Boots: Xen 4.22 + Zephyr Dom0 (xenstore server only — no toolstack, no
# drivers) + dom0less direct-mapped DomD, which owns the display complex, the
# NIC *and* the SD card, and runs the xl toolstack that creates DomU/DomA.
#
# This file is boot.cmd.xen.linux-dom0.in with three differences, so the proven
# address layout stays byte-identical:
#   1. /chosen/dom0 is zephyr.bin instead of the Linux Image, and there is no
#      Dom0 initramfs (Zephyr runs its own xu-create application);
#   2. dom0_mem is sized for Xen's Dom0 bank[0] PLACEMENT, and the address it
#      lands on is a hardware reading rather than a derivation — see the
#      ZEPHYR SRAM RELINK note below;
#   3. the SD card and its expgpio-backed regulators go to DomD, so none of the
#      linux-flavour supply stripping is needed and the slot keeps UHS-I.
#
# The memory map and the Xen bootargs rationale live in
# boot.cmd.xen.linux-dom0.in and are not duplicated here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PHYSICAL MEMORY MAP — identical to the linux flavour except /chosen/dom0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   0x02000000  xen                      0x08000000-0x20000000  DomD bank1 (LOW)
#   0x02200000  xen.dtbo                 0x20000000-0x28000000  Dom0 bank[0] (128M)
#   0x02400000  zephyr.bin               0x40000000-0x80000000  DomD bank0
#   0xa0000000  DomD DTB                 0x80000000-0xa0000000  DomD bank2
#   0xa4000000  DomD kernel Image
#   (0xc0000000  FREE since v93: was the DomD initramfs slot; DomD now boots
#                root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 from the ext4 on SD p2, mounted DIRECTLY
#                because this flavour passes emmc2 through to DomD)
#   4 GiB SKU: DomD bank1 is 0x06000000-0x20000000 and there is no bank2 -- see the
#   board_ram block below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ZEPHYR SRAM RELINK — the one value that must be confirmed on hardware
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Xen cannot pin the hardware/direct-map Dom0 to a DT-specified address:
# construct_hwdom() -> allocate_memory_11() ignores xen,static-mem, which is a
# dom0less-domU-only mechanism. Xen copies the Dom0 image to
# bank[0].start + text_offset, while Zephyr is linked ABSOLUTELY at its
# CONFIG_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS — so if the two disagree Zephyr executes garbage and
# the UART stays silent before console init. That is exactly what happened on
# RPi5 until its SRAM base was relinked from 0x10000000 to 0xc0000000.
#
# allocate_memory_11() (xen/arch/arm/domain_build.c) constrains bank[0] with
#   lowmem_bitsize = min(32, arch_get_dma_bitsize())
# and Xen's rpi4 platform sets .dma_bitsize = 30
# (xen/arch/arm/platforms/brcm-raspberry-pi.c), so on THIS board bank[0] must
# land below 1 GiB — unlike RPi5, which has no platform entry, gets the 32-bit
# default, and therefore placed Dom0 at 0xc0000000.
#
# With the map above TWO naturally-aligned 128 MiB blocks are free below the
# 1 GiB window: 0x20000000 and 0x30000000. (DomD bank1 ends at 0x20000000, the
# firmware leaves the host DT blob at 0x2eff1f00 so the block above 0x28000000
# is not free, and the gpu_mem carve-out starts at 0x3b400000.) Both are in the
# same MEMF_bits tier, so nothing in allocate_memory_11() decides between them
# in a way this file can predict — the full derivation is in
# boot.cmd.xen.linux-dom0.in. bank[0] was MEASURED at
#   *** 0x20000000 ***
# and that is the address to relink Zephyr's sram0 / CONFIG_SRAM_BASE_ADDRESS
# to. dom0_mem below is chosen so the request is one block of that order; the
# address itself rests on the hardware reading below, and on re-reading BANK[0]
# off the Xen console whenever anything in this map changes.
#
# CONFIRMED ON HARDWARE 2026-08-05 (4 GiB board, dom0_mem=128M). The Xen console
# printed EXACTLY:
#   (XEN) Allocating 1:1 mappings totalling 128MB for dom0:
#   (XEN) BANK[0] 0x00000020000000-0x00000028000000 (128MB)
#   (XEN) Loading zImage from 0000000002400000 to 0000000020000000-00000000202da004
# so the predicted placement and the Zephyr link address agree and no relink is
# needed. Note the ADDRESSES ARE PRINTED WITH 14 HEX DIGITS, not the 12 this comment
# used to show: a checker that matched the 12-digit spelling reported FAIL on a board
# whose placement was exactly right and advised relinking Zephyr. Compare numerically.
# If BANK[0] ever differs — a different gpu_mem, a different dom0_mem, or an edited
# memory map all move it — relink Zephyr to whatever the log shows. README.md "Known limitations".
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# BOARD RAM SIZE — 8 GiB (default) or 4 GiB SKU
# =============================================================================
# `setenv board_ram` below is SUBSTITUTED AT BUILD TIME by the xt-rpi-u-boot-scr
# bbappend from ${BOARD_RAM} (moulin --BOARD_RAM 8g|4g, build.sh --ram=8g|4g). It is
# a plain env var, so it can also be overridden at the U-Boot prompt for a one-off
# test:  setenv board_ram 4g ; source ${scriptaddr}
#
# WHY A SWITCH IS NEEDED AT ALL. The RPi4 firmware reports (gpu_mem=76):
#     4 GiB SKU:  0x00000000-0x3b400000 (948 MiB) + 0x40000000-0xfc000000 (3008 MiB)
#                 = 3956 MiB   (there is NO bank above 4 GiB)
#     8 GiB SKU:  the same two + 0x100000000-0x200000000 = 8052 MiB
# The default map is sized for the 8 GiB board. Current values (Dom0 differs by
# flavour: the Zephyr Dom0 is a placement lever at 128 MiB, the Linux Dom0 needs 256
# because it owns emmc2 and every bank must be VideoCore-reachable):
#     8g:  DomD 1920 + Dom0 128..256 + DomU 1024 + DomA 2560 + Xen 80
#          = 5712 MiB (zephyr) / 5840 MiB (linux) of 8052 MiB
# which does not fit 3956 MiB. Dom0+DomD alone DOES fit a 4 GiB board, so
# `board_ram=4g` is not about making the base boot work — it is about leaving room
# for a guest and about not silently over-committing:
#     4g:  DomD 1056 + Dom0 128..256 + Xen 80 = 1264 MiB (zephyr) / 1392
#          (linux), leaving 2692 / 2564 MiB for ONE xl-created guest in the gl
#          lane (the Venus lane below gives DomD 384 MiB more and DomA 512 MiB
#          less).
#          DomU (1024) fits.  DomA (2560) fits ALONE, with 4 MiB to spare on the
#          linux Dom0, which has not been booted (build.sh warns).  The two
#          TOGETHER (3584) do not -- that needs the 8 GiB SKU. build.sh refuses
#          -u together with -a, and -z, on this SKU.
# Xen's 80 MiB is measured, not assumed: `xl info` across three DomD sizes on the
# 4 GiB board gave 78/79/80 MiB of overhead (frametable + xenheap + image).
# tools/check-rpi4-memory-map.py re-derives both configurations from THIS file and
# the host overlay -- banks, their sum against `memory`, containment in real DRAM,
# module load addresses, the two flavours agreeing, and the whole domain budget --
# so the numbers here and there cannot drift apart. It does NOT model
# allocate_memory_11(); Dom0's bank[0] placement below is reasoned, not checked.
setenv board_ram BOARD_RAM_PLACEHOLDER

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VENUS LANE — is this build the Vulkan (Venus) one?
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `setenv venus_lane` below is SUBSTITUTED AT BUILD TIME by the same bbappend, from
# whether 'venus' is in DISTRO_FEATURES (moulin --GPU vulkan, i.e. build.sh's default).
# It is deliberately a SEPARATE axis from board_ram: the delta it causes is not a
# property of the SKU but of what runs on it.
#
# WHY IT CHANGES THE MAP. Venus costs memory in DomD, not in the guest: the
# host-visible blob window is device-model memory in a PCI BAR, so the guest's own
# allocation is untouched. And none of it is reclaimable -- the device model's
# pagemap-sourced blob pages are mlock()ed and the dma-buf ones are pinned by the
# gntdev import, whereas most of DomD's "in use" today is page cache, which is.
# Estimated from the RPi5 blob inventory scaled to DomA's 1920x720: the venus ring
# and shmem pools ~9 MiB, the 16 MiB vn_device_memory suballocation pool, four
# swapchain images at ~5.3 MiB = ~21 MiB, so ~46 MiB of blobs, plus the
# virgl_render_server and V3DV working set (~30-60 MiB, never measured on this
# board) -- call it 76-106 MiB, with a hard ceiling of `hostmem` (256 MiB) plus the
# server.
#
# On the 8 GiB SKU that is noise against DomD's 1920 MiB. On the 4 GiB SKU it is
# not: DomD at 1024 MiB (the earlier map's bank0 640 over a 384 MiB bank1) was
# measured to leave 244 MiB MemFree with DomU's device model running, and bank0 640
# was chosen over 512 (the 896 row below) precisely to keep that
# 244 MiB for DomA's device model, which is bigger (vsock, virtio-serial with six
# virtconsoles, a second NIC) and has never been measured here. Venus would spend
# exactly that reserve.
#
# So on 4g + Venus, move 384 MiB from DomA to DomD: DomD 1440 (1056 + 384), DomA
# 2048. DomA gives up 512 rather than 384 because the other 128 MiB keep its RAM in
# one memory zone (see meta-xt-rpi4's xt-xen-cfg-doma bbappend), so the total goes
# DOWN (80 + 128 + 1440 + 2048 = 3696 of 3956, 260 MiB spare; `xl info` read 262):
# a redistribution, not a new commitment. The blob window was 128 MiB, and
# the transfer was sized at three times that rather than to the estimate because it
# was `hostmem`, the hard upper bound on what the device model can pin -- sizing to
# the bound kept the reserve even if the estimate was wrong. The window is 256 MiB
# now, so the transfer is 1.5 times it and the reserve rests on measurement instead:
# with full-Vulkan AAOS and a video playing in a WebView, 126 MiB of the window in
# use, DomD kept ~505 MiB available (2026-09-24). The asymmetry decides the
# direction: if DomD runs out, weston loses DRM master and BOTH guests' device
# models die with it, while less guest RAM is imperceptible: AAOS at 2048 MiB is
# what upstream sizes it at, and it used 1420 MB with 1080p30 playing (2026-09-23).
# DomA's side of the transfer is in meta-xt-rpi4's xt-xen-cfg-doma bbappend, gated
# the same way.
setenv venus_lane VENUS_LANE_PLACEHOLDER

fdt addr ${fdt_addr}
# NOTE: `fdt resize`'s argument is parsed with hextoul() (u-boot cmd/fdt.c:778),
# so this asks for 0x32768 = 206,184 extra bytes, not 32,768. That is deliberate
# headroom now that it is known: this script performs ~60 `fdt set`/`fdt mknode`
# additions and the DomD/Dom0 module subtrees are created from nothing. Write it as
# 0x8000 if 32 KiB is ever actually wanted.
fdt resize 32768

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Apply the Xen host-DT overlay.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fatload mmc 0 0x2200000 bcm2711-raspberrypi4-64-xen.dtbo
fdt apply 0x2200000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4 GiB SKU: shrink DomD so the map fits 3956 MiB of DRAM.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DomD = 1056 MiB in two banks. bank1 is the low, VideoCore-visible window that
# carries DomD's CMA and sets its ZONE_DMA (of_dma_get_max_cpu_address() takes the
# MINIMUM dma-ranges limit, and the DomD DT's soc_bus caps it at 0x20000000); it
# has to stay below 1 GiB, inside the 0xc0000000 bus alias. On this SKU it starts
# at 0x06000000 rather than 0x08000000, 416 MiB instead of 384 -- see the block
# below. bank2 is dropped and bank0 shrinks 1024 -> 640 MiB.
#
# WHY BANK0 IS 640 MiB AND NOT 1024.
# On a 4 GiB board every guest an xl toolstack creates comes
# out of the SAME 3956 MiB, so DomD's static allocation is the direct budget
# competitor of DomU/DomA. The value is MEASURED, not guessed: DomD was booted at
# three sizes on this board (bank0 1024, 640 and 512 MiB over a 384 MiB bank1)
# with an identical workload (weston + one qemu compositing the AGL cluster on
# HDMI-A-1) [2026-08-04].
#
#   DomD assigned | Xen free_memory | DomD MemFree/Avail | in use | fps (commit/paint)
#   --------------+-----------------+--------------------+--------+-------------------
#      1408 MiB   |     1188 MiB    |     613 / 751 MiB  | 678 MiB|      21 / 18
#      1024 MiB   |     1573 MiB    |     244 / 351 MiB  | 671 MiB|      22 / 16
#       896 MiB   |     1702 MiB    |     161 / 241 MiB  | 628 MiB|      29 / 22
#
# Every row was healthy: no allocation failures, no OOM, no CMA failure (dmesg
# clean), weston kept DRM master on VT7 and the guest surface kept being
# composited. "in use" barely moves because most of the difference is reclaimable
# page cache; the hard floor is ~630 MiB, of which CMA 128 + V3D GEM BOs ~207
# (Shmem) + qemu ~101 + weston ~34. Those rows were measured with cma=128M; DomD
# now reserves 336M on this SKU (see the DomD bootargs), which raises that floor by
# 208 MiB.
#
# Those same runs pin Xen's own overhead, which the older comments guessed at
# "~64 MiB":  3956 - (Dom0 + DomD + DomU) - free_memory = 80 / 79 / 78 MiB across
# the three rows. Use 80.
#
# Bank0 640 (the 1024 row) is chosen over 512 (the 896 row), deliberately: the
# workload above is DomU's device model, and DomA's is BIGGER (doma.cfg adds vsock,
# virtio-serial with SIX virtconsoles and a second NIC on top of the same
# virtio-gpu-gl 1920x720). That delta has never been measured on this board, and
# the consequences are asymmetric -- if DomD runs out, weston loses DRM master and
# BOTH guests' device models die with it, whereas 128 MiB less guest RAM is
# imperceptible. So DomD keeps the 244 MiB of headroom that was measured with a
# guest actually running, and DomA takes the 128 MiB out of its own allocation
# (2560 MiB, still 25% above the 2048 MiB upstream sizes AAOS at).
#
# The 384 MiB that bank0 at 640 frees over 1024 is what makes a 3-domain 4 GiB
# cockpit arithmetically possible at all: 80 (Xen) + 128 (Zephyr Dom0) + 1056
# (DomD, bank1 being 416 MiB on this SKU) = 1264, leaving 2692 MiB for ONE
# xl-created guest. DomU (1024) and DomA still cannot coexist here -- that
# needs the 8 GiB SKU.
#
# Do NOT shrink bank1 to buy more: it is the only VideoCore-reachable window, and
# DomD's CMA (336 MiB on this SKU) plus the V3D scanout buffers live in it.
#
# bank0 at 640 MiB is still far more than place_modules() needs for DomD's
# kernel + DTB (27 MiB + 14 KiB), and the module LOAD addresses (0xa0000000 DTB,
# 0xa4000000 kernel) stay outside every bank, so the copy sources are not clobbered.
#
# Dom0's bank[0] placement is NOT affected: shrinking bank0 only frees memory at
# 0x68000000-0x80000000, which is above the 1 GiB lowmem_bitsize window
# allocate_memory_11() searches. The low map (modules below 0x06000000, DomD bank1
# 0x06000000-0x20000000, the free hole at 0x20000000) leaves the same two 128 MiB
# candidates, 0x20000000 and 0x30000000, and bank[0] was read at 0x20000000 again
# after bank1 moved down to 0x06000000 (2026-09-23). NOT machine-
# checked: tools/check-rpi4-memory-map.py verifies the banks and the budget but
# does not model allocate_memory_11(), so bank[0] at 0x20000000 rests on this
# reasoning plus the hardware observation recorded above.
#
# The `if test` below is safe to rely on: cmd/Makefile:180 is
# `obj-$(CONFIG_HUSH_PARSER) += test.o`, and this u-boot has CONFIG_HUSH_PARSER=y
# (+ HUSH_OLD_PARSER=y), so the `test` command is always present — there is no
# CONFIG_CMD_TEST to forget. That matters because a missing `test` would make the
# condition fail and silently select the 8 GiB map on a 4 GiB board.
#
# tools/check-rpi4-memory-map.py re-derives this override for BOTH flavours and
# fails if they differ, so keep the two boot.cmd files byte-identical in this block.
# It also checks that the Venus sub-block grows only bank@0x40000000 and that DomA
# gives up at least what DomD gains.
setenv domd_cma cma=256M
if test "${board_ram}" = "4g" ; then
    echo "board_ram=4g: DomD 1056 MiB (bank2 dropped, bank0 640 MiB, bank1 416 MiB)"
    fdt set /chosen/domD memory <0x0 0x108000>
    fdt set /chosen/domD xen,static-mem <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x28000000 0x0 0x06000000 0x0 0x1a000000>
    # bank1 starts at 0x06000000 on this SKU, 32 MiB lower than the 8 GiB map's
    # 0x08000000, because that is where more CMA has to come from: the hardware
    # decoder allocates from DomD's CMA, CMA must sit in bank1, and bank1 cannot grow
    # up (Dom0's bank[0] is at 0x20000000). Below it stay the boot modules -- xen at
    # 0x02000000, the overlay at 0x02200000 and the Dom0 image at 0x02400000, which in
    # the linux flavour is a ~26 MiB Image (measured to 0x03dbe9ff) -- so 0x06000000
    # leaves that image 60 MiB. DomD is told about the same window by the soc_bus
    # dma-ranges in bcm2711-raspberrypi4-64-domd-vc4.dts; the two must agree.
    # The 416 MiB are CMA 336 + a 16 MiB swiotlb + 64 MiB of ordinary ZONE_DMA
    # (DomD bootargs below). Measured on the 4 GiB board 2026-09-23, 1080p60 with 13
    # CAPTURE buffers: CmaFree >= 196 MB, no allocation failure. At cma=256M in a
    # 384 MiB bank1 the same run had taken CmaFree to 17 MB and stalled DomD.
    setenv domd_cma "cma=336M swiotlb=8192"
    # 4g + Venus: +384 MiB for the device model's pinned blob memory, taken from
    # DomA (see the venus_lane block above). ONLY bank0 grows -- bank1 is the same
    # 0x06000000+416 MiB in both lanes, it is the only VideoCore-visible window and
    # it carries DomD's CMA and ZONE_DMA. bank0 ends at 0x80000000, where the 8g
    # map's dropped bank2 started, and far above the 1 GiB lowmem window
    # allocate_memory_11() scans for Dom0's bank[0] at 0x20000000 -- so Dom0's
    # placement, the module load addresses (0xa0000000 DTB, 0xa4000000 kernel)
    # and the whole low map are unaffected.
    # HARDWARE DECODE RIDES THIS SAME GATE, and that is deliberate. A 1024 MiB DomD
    # thrashes its page cache during 1080p playback (measured on the board), so the
    # decode path needs this block's 1440 MiB. It is not gated separately
    # because it cannot be: the guest's decoder is a virtio-media device, which only
    # the venus lane's device models (qemu 10.0.2 and 11.1.2) provide. The board
    # yaml sets XT_DOMA_HWDEC from the same GPU parameter, and
    # tools/check-rpi4-memory-map.py asserts the two stay coupled. Do NOT widen this
    # condition to cover a gl-lane hardware-decode build: it would hand the gl lane a
    # DT its device model does not match.
    if test "${venus_lane}" = "yes" ; then
        echo "venus_lane=yes: DomD 1440 MiB (bank0 1024 MiB); DomA drops to 2048"
        fdt set /chosen/domD memory <0x0 0x168000>
        fdt set /chosen/domD xen,static-mem <0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x40000000 0x0 0x06000000 0x0 0x1a000000>
    fi
fi

# dom0_mem is NOT board-dependent in this flavour: 128M is chosen for its
# PLACEMENT (it makes allocate_memory_11() ask for one 128 MiB block below the
# 1 GiB window, and bank[0] was measured at 0x20000000, the Zephyr relink
# target), not for Zephyr's appetite, and the low map that produced that
# reading is identical on both SKUs.
echo "board_ram=${board_ram} dom0_mem=128M (placement-driven, board-independent)"

# XSM Flask is off (xsm=dummy), so no policy module is wanted. Since the overlay's
# compatible was corrected to "multiboot,module" (it said "multiboot-module"), Xen
# would now recognise this node, so this removal is load-bearing rather than a
# no-op. Same treatment as the linux flavour.
fdt rm /chosen/xenpolicy

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dom0 device-ownership fix-ups
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fdt rm /soc/fb

# uart2..uart5 share the 4 KiB page 0xfe201000 with the pl011, which belongs to
# DomD. They still have to go: one owner per page, and an unmarked node makes
# handle_device() route its IRQs to the hardware domain, which would take SPI 121
# away from DomD. See the linux flavour for the full rationale.
fdt rm /soc/serial@7e201400
fdt rm /soc/serial@7e201600
fdt rm /soc/serial@7e201800
fdt rm /soc/serial@7e201a00

# pl011 itself needs nothing here: the Xen host overlay marks &uart0
# `xen,passthrough` so Xen releases SPI 121, and DomD's partial DT claims the node
# with xen,path = "/soc/serial@7e201000" to run hci_uart/hci_bcm on it. Its
# /bluetooth child stays enabled.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SD card -> DomD (the difference that matters versus the linux flavour)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Zephyr Dom0 has no block stack, so DomD owns the SD directly and serves
# /dev/mmcblk0p3 (DomU rootfs) and p4 (DomA super) to the guests as virtio-blk.
# Three things make that work, and of those three only emmc2 needs marking — the
# other two already travel with the mailbox, because the overlay marks
# /soc/firmware. (The Wi-Fi SDIO markers further down this section are a separate
# decision; they are here for the same reason, that the SD/SDIO complex is what
# the two Dom0 flavours disagree about.)
#   emmc2 (/emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000, GIC SPI 126) — marked below, so Xen releases
#     it and DomD's partial DT can claim SPI 126 without route_irq_to_guest
#     returning -EBUSY;
#   expgpio (/soc/firmware/gpio) — the firmware GPIO driving SD_PWR_ON and
#     VDD_SD_IO_SEL, already inside the passthrough'd firmware node;
#   sd_vcc_reg / sd_io_1v8_reg — root-level regulators, pure DT with no MMIO,
#     re-declared in DomD's partial DT.
# Because DomD gets the real regulators it can switch VDD_SD_IO to 1.8 V and keep
# UHS-I — the throughput the linux flavour has to give up.
echo "passthrough: /emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000 (SD -> DomD)"
fdt set /emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000 xen,passthrough

# GIC SPI 126 IS SHARED. On BCM2711 three controllers sit on that one line:
#   /emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000  emmc2  (the SD slot)      -> DomD, marked above
#   /soc/mmcnr@7e300000     sdio   (the onboard WiFi) -> DomD, marked below
#   /soc/mmc@7e300000       sdhci (the legacy SDHCI controller; NOT sdhost - sdhost is /soc/mmc@7e202000 on GIC SPI 120 and stays with Dom0)                    -> removed below
# Xen ignores `status` when deciding ownership, so any /soc node left untouched
# here is assigned to the hardware domain and routes SPI 126 there. DomD would
# then ask for the same SPI, route_irq_to_guest() would return -EBUSY, and DomD
# construction aborts with no other diagnostic. So each of the three has to be
# dealt with explicitly.
#
# mmcnr is the onboard Wi-Fi SDIO controller and it goes to DomD, which needs it
# to give DomA a network to browse from: brcmfmac is already in the DomD image,
# and so is its Cypress firmware when the build accepts synaptics-killswitch
# (README, *Wi-Fi firmware licence*), and neither has a device to bind to
# otherwise. Two notes on why this is `fdt set`:
#
#   * It MUST be `fdt set`, not `fdt rm`. DomD's partial DT reaches this device
#     with xen,path = "/soc/mmcnr@7e300000", and handle_passthrough_prop()
#     resolves that path against the HOST DT (dt_find_node_by_path). Delete the
#     node and the lookup returns NULL, which is -EINVAL and panics domain
#     construction. `fdt set` is also what makes Xen release the SPI, which is
#     the whole point.
#
#   * DomD then names SPI 126 twice, once via emmc2 and once via mmcnr, and that
#     is legal. route_irq_to_guest() returns -EBUSY only for a different domain,
#     a different virq on the same line, or a line Xen itself uses; same domain
#     plus same virq falls through with retval 0, and dom0less passthrough always
#     uses virq == irq. The requirement is that both partial-DT nodes declare the
#     SAME trigger type, because irq_set_spi_type() accepts a repeat only when
#     curr == new. Both use <0 126 4>. Linux is fine with it too: sdhci requests
#     its IRQ with IRQF_SHARED.
#
# /soc/mmc@7e300000 is a second, status="disabled" description of the very same
# Arasan controller mmcnr describes, so it has no user and is removed -- leaving
# it would hand SPI 126 to the hardware domain and undo the two `fdt set`s above.
echo "passthrough: /soc/mmcnr@7e300000 (onboard WiFi SDIO -> DomD, shares SPI 126)"
fdt set /soc/mmcnr@7e300000 xen,passthrough
echo "rm: /soc/mmc@7e300000 (disabled duplicate of mmcnr, would take SPI 126)"
fdt rm /soc/mmc@7e300000

# mmcnr's DMA engine. The Arasan SDHCI block mmcnr sits on has no usable internal
# bus master, so its only route to DMA is the EXTERNAL legacy engine, which the
# host wires up as dmas = <&dma-controller@7e007000 11> (DREQ 11). Without this
# marker bcm2835-mmc.c cannot get a channel and falls back to PIO, which costs
# about three times the interrupts for the same transfers (16105-16701 against
# 4487-6533 over three repeats of a fixed 609 KB firmware load).
#
# THE NODE NAME IS dma-controller@7e007000, not dma@7e007000. Measured in the
# shipped bcm2711-rpi-4-b.dtb. xen,path is resolved against the HOST DT with
# dt_find_node_by_path(), so a wrong spelling returns NULL and panics domain
# construction with -EINVAL.
#
# `fdt set`, never `fdt rm`, for the same reason as mmcnr above.
#
# The page 0xfe007000 is shared with dma40 (/scb/dma@7e007b00, HDMI audio and the
# vchiq probe), which DomD also takes; its marker is in the Xen host overlay
# because both Dom0 flavours give it to DomD. The two register windows do not
# overlap. See the notes on legacy_dma_bus and dma40 in
# bcm2711-raspberrypi4-64-domd-vc4.dts.
#
# BOTH THIS AND THE mmcnr MARKER ABOVE STAY IN THE BOOT SCRIPT rather than moving
# to the Xen host overlay where every other ownership decision lives: the overlay
# is one dtbo applied by both Dom0 flavours, and these two devices are exactly the
# flavour-specific case it cannot express. In the linux flavour Dom0 owns emmc2
# and SPI 126, mmcnr is absent from DomD (domd-vc4.bb strips it together with its
# DMA engine), and the whole SD/SDIO complex stays with Dom0.
echo "passthrough: /soc/dma-controller@7e007000 (legacy DMA -> DomD, Wi-Fi SDIO DREQ 11)"
fdt set /soc/dma-controller@7e007000 xen,passthrough

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drop the host CMA reservation and any VideoCore framebuffer leftovers.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never rewrite /reserved-memory itself: the BCM2711 root is #size-cells=<1> and
# a cells mismatch makes Linux discard the whole node, including the atf@0
# no-map entry that protects TF-A.
fdt rm /reserved-memory/linux,cma
fdt rm /chosen/framebuffer
fdt rm /chosen/framebuffer@3f800000
fdt rm /reserved-memory/framebuffer
fdt rm /framebuffer@3f800000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Xen hypervisor bootargs
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dom0_mem=128M: Zephyr itself needs only a few MiB, but the value is chosen for
# its PLACEMENT, not its size — it makes allocate_memory_11() request one
# 128 MiB-aligned 128 MiB block below 1 GiB. The map above leaves two such
# blocks free and bank[0] was measured at 0x20000000. Changing dom0_mem changes
# the order, and with it the set of candidate addresses, so it invalidates the
# Zephyr relink: keep the two in lockstep (see ZEPHYR SRAM RELINK above).
#
# WHY 128 AND NOT 256 (changed 2026-08-04), AND WHY NOT LESS:
#   * 256M cannot be satisfied as ONE block on this board. The firmware places the
#     host DT blob at 0x2eff1f00 (observed: MODULE[1] 0x2eff1f00-0x2f000fff), which
#     sits inside 0x20000000-0x30000000, so allocate_memory_11() halves the order
#     and Dom0 ends up with 128 MiB @0x20000000 + 128 MiB @0x30000000 -- two banks
#     with a hole between them, while the overlay declared one 256 MiB region.
#     128M asks for exactly the first of those, so the declaration matches reality.
#   * It frees 128 MiB. On the 4 GiB SKU that is 128 MiB more for the xl-created
#     guest, which is the whole point of the 4 GiB cockpit budget.
#   * 64M or 32M do NOT work. The scan is for a NATURALLY ALIGNED block, so a
#     smaller order brings LOWER holes in as CANDIDATES, and those are worse
#     places for Dom0 to land:
#         32 MiB -> 0x00000000 becomes a candidate  (config.txt loads
#                                armstub=bl31.bin there; TF-A BL31 and the
#                                secondary-CPU spin tables live in it)
#         64 MiB -> 0x04000000 becomes a candidate  (the gap between the boot
#                                modules and DomD bank1; no evidence it is
#                                unused, and Zephyr would have to be relinked)
#        128 MiB -> the candidates are 0x20000000 and 0x30000000, and bank[0]
#                                was measured at 0x20000000 (the hole this map
#                                deliberately leaves)
#     A smaller order does not GUARANTEE the lower address -- the pick inside one
#     MEMF_bits tier is not predictable -- but it makes those addresses reachable,
#     which on its own is reason enough not to shrink dom0_mem.
#     Dom0's size is a PLACEMENT LEVER on this board, not a memory requirement.
#     Nothing models this scan for BCM2711 and nothing fails the build if
#     rpi_4b.overlay's sram0 base disagrees with it: tools/check-rpi4-memory-map.py
#     checks this board's banks and budget but not allocate_memory_11(), and the
#     BCM2712 tool has no rpi4 rows. The Zephyr board patch says the same thing
#     (0019-boards-rpi_4b-zephyr-dom0-board.patch) -- read BANK[0] off the Xen
#     console on the first boot; a mismatch is total UART silence.
fdt set /chosen xen,xen-bootargs "console=dtuart dtuart=/soc/serial@7e215040 dom0_mem=128M dom0_max_vcpus=1 xsm=dummy gnttab_max_frames=512 bootscrub=off loglvl=all guest_loglvl=all sync_console"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Load Xen
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
fatload mmc 0 0x2000000 xen
echo "Xen loaded at 0x2000000, size 0x${filesize}"

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Zephyr Dom0
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No bootargs and no initramfs: Zephyr ignores both. Xen still needs the module
# `reg` so it knows where to copy the image from. (On RPi5 an inherited
# fatload of the Linux Dom0 initramfs left module@1 declared with a junk size —
# do not re-add that block here.)
fatload mmc 0 0x2400000 zephyr.bin
fdt set /chosen/dom0 reg <0x0 0x2400000 0x0 0x${filesize}>

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dom0less DomD (direct-map + static-mem)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# [v93] DomD no longer boots from a RAM initramfs. Its root is the ext4 on SD p2,
# mounted DIRECTLY (this flavour passes emmc2 through to DomD), so nothing is fatloaded
# for it beyond the kernel and its partial DT, and there is no module@2 ramdisk. The gate
# for "is DomD deployed" is therefore the KERNEL load, not the initramfs load.
if fatload mmc 0 0xa4000000 Image ; then
    setenv domd_kernel_size ${filesize}
    fatload mmc 0 0xa0000000 bcm2711-raspberrypi4-64-domd-vc4.dtb
    setenv domd_dtb_size ${filesize}

    # No `xen,domain-id`: not a Xen 4.21 dom0less binding (see the linux flavour).
    # DomD is the first /chosen domain child, so it is domid 1 by allocation order.
    # DOMAIN_CAPS_CONTROL: DomD runs the toolstack in this flavour, so it needs
    # the privileged sysctls xl / xl devd issue.
    fdt set /chosen/domD capabilities <0x1>

    fdt mknode /chosen/domD module@0
    fdt set /chosen/domD/module@0 compatible "multiboot,kernel" "multiboot,module"
    fdt set /chosen/domD/module@0 reg <0x0 0xa4000000 0x0 0x${domd_kernel_size}>
    # `xen_privcmd.unrestricted=1` is what lets DomD run `xl`: the carried privcmd
    # patch blocks every hypercall in a non-initial domain otherwise. It is silently
    # IGNORED if the kernel is locked down (security_locked_down(
    # LOCKDOWN_XEN_USER_ACTIONS) in restrict_driver()), so bcm2711-domd-hw.cfg
    # asserts `# CONFIG_SECURITY_LOCKDOWN_LSM is not set`. Change one, change both.
    # [v93] rdinit=/init-vc4.sh is gone (init-vc4.sh was deleted upstream); weston now
    # runs from the stock poky weston.service with GPU bring-up in domd-gpu-init.service,
    # and DomD's root is the ext4 on SD p2. cma 192M -> 128M for the same reason (no
    # initramfs to fit).
    #
    # root=/dev/mmcblk0p2, NOT /dev/xvda. THIS IS THE ONE LINE THAT DIFFERS FROM THE
    # linux FLAVOUR, and getting it wrong is silent: DomD's kernel boots fine, brings up
    # ttyAMA0 (it even echoes characters back when Xen's console focus is switched to
    # DOM1), and then sits in rootwait forever with no userspace, no network and no login
    # prompt. Measured on hardware 2026-08-05 with root=/dev/xvda here.
    #   zephyr flavour  DomD owns emmc2 -- `fdt set /emmc2bus/mmc@7e340000 xen,passthrough`
    #                   above hands the SD slot to DomD, so it mounts p2 DIRECTLY.
    #   linux  flavour  Dom0 owns emmc2 and DomD gets p2 over PV block as xvda, supplied
    #                   by Dom0's xl-attach-disks.service (`xl block-attach 1
    #                   phy:/dev/mmcblk0p2,xvda,w`).
    # There is NO blkback in a Zephyr Dom0 -- it runs xu-create and a xenstore server and
    # nothing else -- so xvda can never appear in this flavour. Do not copy a root= change
    # from one flavour to the other; v93 was applied to both and that is how this got in.
    # rootfstype=ext4 skips the probe list, rootwait covers the mmc probe finishing after
    # the rootfs lookup, rw is required (systemd and sshd write to the root).
    #
    # cma=256M: hardware H.264 decode takes its buffers from DomD's CMA, which lives in
    # bank1, the only VideoCore-visible window. At 128M a 1080p30 stream exhausted it
    # (measured 2026-09-15: "bcm2835-codec: dma alloc of size 3133440 failed", cma_alloc
    # -EBUSY for 765 pages, then an order-10 GFP_DMA reclaim storm that stalled DomD for
    # minutes). With 256M three consecutive 1080p30 runs passed with cma_alloc_fail 0
    # and CmaFree never below 116 MB. It pairs with the guest's
    # debug.v4l2codec2.output_delay=2 (11 CAPTURE buffers instead of 25), which the
    # rpi4 device's product makefile sets.
    # ${domd_cma} is that cma=256M on the 8 GiB map, where 256 + the 64 MiB swiotlb
    # leave 64 MiB of bank1's 384 as ordinary ZONE_DMA. The 4 GiB map sets
    # `cma=336M swiotlb=8192` for its 416 MiB bank1 (see the board_ram block above).
    # A bigger DomD does not help here unless bank1 grows: bank0 is not VideoCore-
    # visible. The expanded line is 181 chars on the 4 GiB map; U-Boot's
    # CONFIG_SYS_CBSIZE is 1024.
    fdt set /chosen/domD/module@0 bootargs "console=ttyAMA0 root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 rootfstype=ext4 rootwait rw clk_ignore_unused vhost_xen.nogrant=1 xen_privcmd.unrestricted=1 ${domd_cma} net.ifnames=0 quiet loglevel=3"

    fdt mknode /chosen/domD module@1
    fdt set /chosen/domD/module@1 compatible "multiboot,device-tree" "multiboot,module"
    fdt set /chosen/domD/module@1 reg <0x0 0xa0000000 0x0 0x${domd_dtb_size}>


    echo "DomD dom0less + direct-map + GPU/SD passthrough configured (dtb@0xa0000000 / kernel@0xa4000000, root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 direct)"
else
    fdt rm /chosen/domD
    echo "DomD kernel not on SD; Dom0-only boot (dom0less DomD disabled)"
fi

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# dom0less DomU — disabled; DomU and DomA are created by DomD's xl.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
setenv domu_loaded 0
if test "${domu_loaded}" = "1" ; then
    echo "dom0less DomU is not implemented on rpi4 yet"
else
    fdt rm /chosen/domU
fi

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hand off to Xen
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do not let U-Boot fix up the DT after we finished editing it.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `booti` calls image_setup_libfdt() -> ft_board_setup()
# (board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c:577), which runs AFTER every `fdt rm` above and
# unconditionally adds a root-level `/framebuffer` node via
# fdt_simplefb_add_node(). The node is added with status = "disabled"
# (boot/fdt_simplefb.c:63; fdt_setup_simplefb_node() never writes status), so no
# simplefb driver binds it — but it does carry a `reg` in the VideoCore carve-out
# that Xen's handle_node() would then map into Dom0's p2m, and it silently
# reintroduces a node this script just deleted.
#
# boot/image-fdt.c:631-634 honours `skip_board_fixup=1` and skips ft_board_setup()
# entirely. What that also skips is update_fdt_from_fw(), which copies
# /chosen/kaslr-seed and the ethernet PHY `reg` from the firmware DT into this
# blob. Neither matters here: Xen rebuilds /chosen for Dom0 from scratch
# (domain_build.c), and DomD does not inherit this tree at all — it gets its own
# partial DT, which declares genet with its own mdio/phy nodes.
#
# The u-boot cfg fragment additionally drops CONFIG_VIDEO/VIDEO_BCM2835, so
# U-Boot never asks the VideoCore for a framebuffer either. This line is the
# belt to that suspenders: it holds even if a future defconfig re-enables video.
setenv skip_board_fixup 1

setenv fdt_high 0xffffffffffffffff
# Mux GPIO30-33 to ALT3 (pl011 CTS0/RTS0/TXD0/RXD0) before Xen starts.
#
# Measured in U-Boot on the board: the firmware leaves these four pins as plain
# inputs (GPFSEL3 reads 0x3FFFF000), and a config.txt `gpio=` line only reaches
# GPIO32/33 -- GPIO30/31 stay 0. DomD's partial DT asserts uart-has-rtscts, so
# without RTS0 the controller never answers (hci0: command 0xfc18 tx timeout).
# DomD cannot do the mux itself: the GPIO block at 0xfe200000 is not passed
# through and DomD has no pinctrl for it. So it happens here, in the last stage
# that still owns the whole address space.
#
# Read-modify-write, so GPIO34-39 (the SDIO Wi-Fi pins, already ALT3 from the
# firmware) are left untouched: GPFSEL3 bits 0-11 -> 0b111 per pin; pulls 30 up /
# 31 none in PUP_PDN_CNTRL_REG1 bits 28-31, 32 none / 33 up in
# PUP_PDN_CNTRL_REG2 bits 0-3 -- upstream's uart0_pins plus uart0_ctsrts_pins.
# Hush requires the operators escaped as \| and \&; an unescaped | is a pipe and
# aborts the script.
#
# Verified on the board: with GPFSEL3 reading back 0x3FFFFFFF the controller
# answers (chip id 107, BCM4345C0 build 0382); with GPIO32/33 alone it does not.
setexpr.l btgpf *0xfe20000c \| 0x00000fff
mw.l 0xfe20000c ${btgpf} 1
setexpr.l btpup1 *0xfe2000e8 \& 0x0fffffff
setexpr.l btpup1 ${btpup1} \| 0x10000000
mw.l 0xfe2000e8 ${btpup1} 1
setexpr.l btpup2 *0xfe2000ec \& 0xfffffff0
setexpr.l btpup2 ${btpup2} \| 0x00000004
mw.l 0xfe2000ec ${btpup2} 1

booti 0x2000000 - ${fdt_addr}
